# Phase 0 checks for the API skeleton (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above a block).
# Start the API first: npm run dev:api

@api = http://localhost:4000/api

### Health: 200 { "ok": true, "time": <millis> }
GET {{api}}/health

### Unknown route: 404 { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "Not found.", "meta": {} }
GET {{api}}/walang-ito

### Malformed JSON: 400 { "code": "INVALID", "message": "The request body is not valid JSON.", "meta": {} }
POST {{api}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

{bad json

### CORS, allowed portal: the response has Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:5173
GET {{api}}/health
Origin: http://localhost:5173

### CORS, other origin: the response has NO Access-Control-Allow-Origin header (a browser would block it)
GET {{api}}/health
Origin: http://localhost:4173
